@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# Markdown (.md) upload cases for POST /api/content-bank/assets/upload.
# All requests require authentication — run "Login" from sessions/sessions.http first.
#
# Limit: 10 MB per .md file.
# Fixtures in this directory: sample.md, sample2.md, rust-learning-plan.md.

### Upload Markdown — single file  [protected]
# @name uploadMarkdown
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="rust-learning-plan.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./rust-learning-plan.md
--boundary--

> {% client.global.set("mdAssetId", response.body.results[0].asset_id) %}

### Upload Markdown — multiple files (batch)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./sample.md
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample2.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./sample2.md
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="rust-learning-plan.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./rust-learning-plan.md
--boundary--

### Upload Markdown — mixed valid + non-.md (per-file failure, 201)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./sample.md
--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

just plain text, not markdown
--boundary--

### Upload Markdown — no files (expects 400)  [protected]
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary--

### Upload Markdown — unauthenticated (expects 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/content-bank/assets/upload
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="files"; filename="sample.md"
Content-Type: text/markdown

< ./sample.md
--boundary--
